  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_zcjHMGnpDkQvZpXP",
   "name": "Saturated & unsaturated Compounds",
   "definition": "State that a saturated compound has molecules in which all carbon–carbon bonds are single bonds\nState that an unsaturated compound has molecules in which one or more carbon–carbon bonds are not single bonds"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Saturated & unsaturated Compounds"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What are saturated compounds?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Saturated compounds** are molecules with only **single carbon-carbon bonds **(C-C)\n\n  - Each carbon atom has 4 single bonds to other atoms\n- **Alkanes** are examples of saturated compounds ** **\n- Alkanes have the general formula **C**<sub>**n**</sub>**H**<sub>**2n+2**</sub>\n- The first three alkanes are:"
  },
  {
   "type": "ordered",
   "md": "1. Methane, CH<sub>4</sub>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/02/methane.png",
   "file": "assets/2a3003e806a7-methane.png",
   "alt": "methane",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "ordered",
   "md": "2. Ethane, C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/02/ethane.png",
   "file": "assets/21ec4d0a4ee6-ethane.png",
   "alt": "ethane",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "ordered",
   "md": "3. Propane, C<sub>3</sub>H<sub>8</sub>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/02/propane.png",
   "file": "assets/625c09c3e966-propane.png",
   "alt": "propane",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What are unsaturated compounds?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Unsaturated compounds** are molecules with one or more carbon-carbon **double bonds** (C=C)\n\n  - Each carbon atom has 4 bonds to other atoms\n  - But, one bond is a double bond\n- **Alkenes** are examples of unsaturated compounds ** **\n- Alkenes have the general formula **C**<sub>**n**</sub>**H**<sub>**2n**</sub>\n- The first three alkenes are:"
  },
  {
   "type": "ordered",
   "md": "1. Ethene, C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>4</sub>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/02/ethene.png",
   "file": "assets/c905b447320d-ethene.png",
   "alt": "ethene",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "ordered",
   "md": "2. Propene, C<sub>3</sub>H<sub>6</sub>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/02/propene.png",
   "file": "assets/b9fdeaaf358a-propene.png",
   "alt": "propene",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "ordered",
   "md": "3. Butene, C<sub>4</sub>H<sub>8</sub>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/02/but-1-ene.png",
   "file": "assets/3bd75c6173ba-but-1-ene.png",
   "alt": "but-1-ene",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "**Remember:**\n\n**S**aturated compounds have **S**ingle bonds only.\n\n**U**nsaturated compounds have do**U**ble bonds"
  }
 ]
}